@gitlab: No "we" here, as this would indicate staff participation in this action, etc., which is neither likely, nor logical. Also, "them" serves no purpose in this specific instance, where "unban the user"/"unban this user" should've clearly been used instead:
>> "Because you've enabled auto-banning, this user has also been automatically banned from %{scope}. If this is a mistake, you can %{link_start}unban this user%{link_end}.".
This is a classic mistake of using active voice, believing that active voice actually serves a logical purpose or contributes positively to all UI texts. In this case, active voice is only misleading the user, this phrasing achieves nothing else in a positive sensea.

@gitlab:
Same basic misuse of active voice as already outlined on source string #110157:

>> "Because you enabled auto-banning, this user has also been automatically banned from the %{scope}. If this is a mistake, you can unban the user: %{url}.".

