@WP_requests  the short answer is, please keep the English format, do not localize the format.

Here is why (based on the code in the original request - https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/merge_requests/194297):

GitLab has backend validation that checks the format of time duration inputs. When a user enters a value like "30 m" (with a space) instead of "30m" (without a space), the system will reject the input and show an error message. This validation works the same way regardless of what language the user has selected in GitLab's interface, because the system checks the actual characters typed, not translated text. The validation uses a specific pattern in the code, a regex like this: \A([1-9]\d*)([mhd])\z.  If the format is wrong, the user will see an error message telling them the correct format to use, and they will need to fix their input before the system will accept it.

