@SabrinaDeVellis @FKP  in this merge request, https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/merge_requests/191015 , "target" is being used as a verb in the branch selection options. It's indicating an action - to select or focus on specific branches for scan execution.

For example, in "target all protected branches", "target" means to select or apply the scan to all protected branches. Similarly, in "target default branch" or "target all default branches", it's instructing the scan execution policy to focus on those specific branches.

So "target" is indeed a verb in this context, not a complement. It's describing the action of selecting or focusing on specific branches for the scan execution policy to be applied to.

